From 62c92a1b7c719ceb59dfe1947637dfa3ecefab8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 02:23:39 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] kcm_kup: probe bup/rsync asynchronously, restore button
 in the top row, 'Advanced' page renamed
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Page type: List (QtWidgets, docs/page-design.md 8: kept in QtWidgets, the plan editor is a 2500-line widget set with config managers, not a small port).
kuprc keys, plan numbering, save/reload logic and the daemon call are unchanged.

Speed cause (code): the KcmKup constructor ran three processes synchronously, 'bup version', 'bup fsck --par2-ok' and 'rsync --version'
(kupkcm.cpp:39,44,52 before this commit), so the first frame waited on process start-ups (and on bup's python start). They now run with QProcess
and signals; the page shows 'Looking for backup programs…' and finishSetup() builds the real page (or the 'Backup programs are missing' page)
when both probes have answered, then calls load(). load()/save() return early until then. Still synchronous and left as is: BackupPlanWidget
(five KPageWidget pages, folder tree, Solid drive list in driveselection.cpp:55) is built for every plan inside load(); a lazy build on Configure would
be the next step, not done because the config manager of each plan needs its widget. After-numbers: pending, manager will measure.

Moved / renamed:
- Front page top row: 'Backups enabled', then 'Restore From Backup…' (was the button 'Open and restore from existing backups' at the bottom
  of the plan list, so it was below any number of plans; old text is the tooltip) and 'Add New Plan…'. Rows kcm_kup/OpenRestore, AddPlan.
- Plan card: 'Configure' -> 'Configure…' (opens the plan page). Plan page: 'Back to overview' -> 'Back to Plans', 'Description:' -> 'Plan name:'.
- Plan page list entry 'Advanced' ('Extra options for advanced users', icon preferences-other) -> 'Exclusions and Checks' ('Choose what to leave out and
  how backups are checked', icon view-filter) (HIG-057). The options on it are unchanged.
- Markers added on the changed and weak rows; relabel: inventory/relabel/kcm_kup.tsv. Inventory --strict: 0 lost.
HIG ids: HIG-001/005/006, HIG-019, HIG-057, HIG-058.
Not built yet. Unconfirmed without a build: late KCModule::addConfig() after construction (done in finishSetup) registers the KConfigDialogManager
and change tracking like the early call did; QProcess::errorOccurred(FailedToStart) may fire inside start(), so mProbesPending starts at 2 and is
not reset; QProcess::finished(int, ExitStatus) signal (Qt 6).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
